Small/Medium/Moderate/Large ADV raid complexes spawn in insurgency systems with these properties:
- per-size ship restrictions;
- capture timers of 10 or 15 minutes;
- per-site corruption/suppression contribution of 0.25/0.5/1.5/1%;
- Moderate sites grant a battlecruiser bonus;
- Large ADV is static with a 40-min respawn.
Mordu's Legion NPCs defend for pirates and pirate NPCs for empires.

dungeonInstanceCacheMgr.GetPirateInsurgencyIceHeistInstances lists heists. Spawn rules: only at corruption 3–4, with a 4h respawn that persists across downtime.

In the site:
- tanker NPCs spawn at the refinery and are web-immune;
- each side escorts them to its own scoring zone;
- the first side to 10 tankers wins 150,000 LP;
- pirates near the Upwell Thunderchild guards are destroyed.

A covert cyno:
- requires Cynosural Field Theory V and fits only covert-cloak-capable hulls (plus Etana/Prospect/Rabisu);
- uses 1/10 of normal cycle time and fuel (25 LO);
- is visible only to ships on grid;
- can be lit in cyno-jammed systems;
- can be jumped to or bridged only by Black Ops.

Industrial cynos:
- fit only on the Venture (50% LO role bonus), haulers, blockade runners and DSTs;
- use 800 LO per cycle base, 400 minimum with CFT V;
- appear on the overview;
- can be jumped to only by jump freighters, capital industrials and Black Ops; Rorqual and Black Ops may also bridge to them.

Show-info on a wormhole returns:
- destination class text (C1-3, C4-5, C6, High/Low/Null, Triglavian, Drifter, Thera);
- maximum ship size category (Small/Medium/Large/Extra large);
- reliable lifetime bucket (<1 day, <4 h, <1 h, expired);
- mass stability bucket (>50%, <50%, <10%).

All values are derived from live wormhole state.

A 10 s session change timer starts on any of:
- login, stargate/wormhole/jump bridge jump or jump drive use;
- dock or undock;
- fleet join or position change;
- ejecting, ship loss or podding, or boarding a ship;
- clone jump or clone swap;
- corp join or leave, or a corp wallet division change.

While it runs, further session-changing actions are refused or queued per the live error behaviour.

During the 60 s post-jump cloak (stargate or wormhole), the ship:
- is not visible on grid;
- takes no damage from bombs, smartbombs or ECM bursts;
- cannot be decloaked by proximity or bumped.

Any action ends the cloak.

Remote assistance:
- of suspects or outlaws is a suspect offence;
- of criminals is a criminal offence;
- that interferes in a war or limited engagement is criminal in high-sec and suspect in low-sec.

Command burst effects are filtered by the same legality in high-sec.

In low-sec:
- attacking a capsuleer ship (including with untargeted smartbombs) gives a suspect flag, not criminal;
- attacking a capsule gives a criminal flag;
- neither spawns CONCORD; sentry guns respond;
- jumping into high-sec within the 15 min criminal timer triggers CONCORD.

At security status −4.95 or below, a character is an outlaw:
- anyone may attack them anywhere without CONCORD response or penalty;
- remote assistance to them is a suspect offence, even for corp members;
- assisting outlaws in low-sec is not an offence.

Tethering is refused for:
- characters without docking rights;
- ships warp-disrupted below 0 WCS;
- ships with a weapons timer or with fighters launched and not abandoned;
- unpiloted ships (capsules tether immediately);
- structures without a quantum core, or in the abandoned state.

Tether breaks on:
- locking a target;
- launching fighters;
- leaving the 10 km-from-docking-ring range;
- activating a burst jammer, command burst, cyno, siege, triage or bastion module.

While tethered, smartbombs, bomb launchers and fleet ore compression are refused.

An abyssal filament admits one of:
- one T1/T2/navy/pirate cruiser, but no strategic cruisers;
- up to two destroyers, consuming 2 filaments (T3 destroyers allowed);
- up to three frigates, consuming 3 filaments.

Frigate and destroyer traces can be activated only by fleet members.

Filament activation is refused:
- within 1,000 km of a gate, station, mobile depot or another Abyssal Trace;
- inside a deadspace pocket;
- with an active capsuleer log-off timer;
- while post-warp invulnerable.

Each refusal uses the live error.

Inside an abyssal pocket:
- no warping in or out, no cloaking and no mobile depots;
- no Local channel; directional scan and map are disabled;
- probes outside the pocket boundary take damage;
- ships and capsules entering the boundary zone are destroyed.

At downtime, players in a pocket return to the origin system and drones in space are lost.

Bastion has a 60 s cycle. While active:
- turret/launcher cycle time -50% (not stacking-penalised);
- missile velocity, turret optimal and falloff +25% (stacking-penalised);
- local repair/boost amount +60%, and repair/boost cycle time and capacitor cost -20%;
- shield, armor and hull resists +30%, stacking with Damage Control and Reactive Armor Hardener;
- sensor strength +100%, but NO ECM immunity;
- velocity -100%, and the ship cannot dock, tether or warp;
- a 60 s weapons timer, refreshed throughout the cycle;
- no incoming remote repair or capacitor, and friendly Remote Sensor Booster/Remote Tracking Computer effects are reduced 95%.

Activation rules:
- one Entosis Link per ship; each cycle consumes 1 Strontium Clathrates;
- the link needs a locked target and has no effect outside the target's vulnerability window;
- Interceptors cannot activate it.

While the link is active:
- the ship cannot cloak, warp, dock or jump;
- capital ships get a 5x cycle time and cannot receive remote assistance.

While the link is online, the ship's speed is capped at 4,000 m/s. These restrictions end only when the cycle finishes or the ship is lost.

Audit log secure containers and station containers record these events with actor and time:
- assembly;
- each lock and unlock, with the stack quantity at that moment;
- password changes;
- successful and failed password entries;
- configuration changes;
- renames.
The log is retrievable by the owner or corporation. Containers can be configured to lock inserted items by default and to require a password per action. A container with log entries younger than 3 weeks cannot be repackaged, reprocessed or trashed.

Starting research with an R&D agent requires:
- Science V;
- Mechanics V, Power Grid Management V or CPU Management V;
- the agent's field skill;
- being docked in the agent's station.
The number of concurrent R&D agents is 1 + Research Project Management level, up to 6. Access needs both of these:
- the normal effective standing for the agent level toward the agent, its corporation or its faction (5.0 for level 4);
- effective corporation standing at least 2.0 below that requirement (3.0 for level 4).
In particular, faction standing 10 with corporation standing 0 is refused.

Ice harvester cycle duration is reduced by these modifiers, applied via dogma:
- the Ice Harvesting skill, per level;
- Ice Harvester Upgrade modules (not stacking-penalised: SDE duration attribute 73 has stackable=1);
- barge, exhumer and ICS hull bonuses;
- ice mining crystals or rigs, where applicable.
Each cycle still yields exactly one ice block.

Activation and requirements:
- usable only while the Lancer's siege module is active;
- needs Disruptive Lance Operation (-5% capacitor per level);
- the Lancer Dreadnoughts skill gives +10% lance damage and +20% range per level;
- allowed in low-sec.
On activation:
- deals one third of Titan-lance damage;
- neutralises 10,000 GJ from ships in the area;
- disables docking, jumping, tethering, stargate use and warping for affected ships;
- halves their incoming remote repair.
The firing Lancer cannot jump, dock, tether or cloak for 5 min, and a Lancer with a lance fitted cannot activate cloaks.

Activation: 5-minute cycle consuming 250 - 25*Tactical Weapon Reconfiguration Strontium Clathrates. Activation gives no weapons timer.
While active:
- turret damage +700% (T2 +840%), missile damage +165% (T2 +200%);
- XL cruise and torpedo cycle -80%, torpedo velocity +150%;
- sensor dampener and weapon disruption resistance 60% (T2 70%), 80% remote assistance impedance, ECM immunity;
- local repair amount +100% and duration -50%;
- mass x10, velocity -100% (the Sarathiel keeps part of its speed via its hull bonus);
- no remote repair or capacitor can be received.

Activation: 5-minute cycle consuming 200 - 25*Tactical Logistics Reconfiguration Strontium Clathrates.
While active:
- capital remote repair amount +400% (T2 +450%), duration -75%, range +200%;
- scan resolution +900%, max locked targets +4 (T2 +5);
- local repair duration -50% and amount +100% (T2 +120%), with capacitor cost unchanged;
- sensor dampener resistance 60% (T2 70%), 80% remote assistance impedance, ECM immunity;
- mass x10, velocity -100%, drone damage -100%;
- EWAR modules disabled;
- no remote repair or capacitor can be received.

Launcher limits:
- only one Interdiction Sphere Launcher can be fitted;
- it fires one probe per 5 s, reloads in 60 s and holds 3 probes;
- it is refused in empire space except low-sec systems at corruption stage 5.
Probes:
- a Warp Disrupt Probe makes a 20 km bubble lasting 2 min; a Surgical probe makes a 10 km bubble lasting 3 min;
- probes take no targeted damage, only bombs and smartbombs hurt them;
- launching does not create aggression.
Bubbles:
- stop warps initiated inside them, except logoff warps;
- block capital cyno jumps out;
- shuttles and ships with an active Interdiction Nullifier are immune.

Reprocessing in an Upwell structure uses that structure type's base yield before skills, implants and rigs:
- Citadels and Engineering Complexes: 50%;
- Athanor: 51%;
- Tatara: 52%.

The value comes from SDE data. reprocessingSvc quotes report it, and the reprocessed output reflects it.

Each Mining Foreman Burst charge applies only its own dbuff to fleet members within burst range:
- Mining Laser Optimization: mining module duration and capacitor use, base -15%;
- Mining Laser Field Enhancement: mining and survey module range bonus;
- Mining Laser Efficiency: lower residue probability and higher mining critical-success chance.

Strength scales with:
- T2 module (+25%);
- Mining Director (+10%/level);
- mindlink and industrial core.

Duration scales with Mining Foreman (+10%/level). A burst loaded with one charge type grants none of the other charges' effects.

Launcher:
- Survey Probe Launcher, one per ship, needs no hardpoint;
- does not auto-repeat, but auto-reloads.

Launching:
- the probe must be launched aligned at a moon within 100,000 km;
- a probe that misses returns no result;
- probes are consumed and cannot be recalled.

Results:
- arrive after the probe's flight time (T2 launcher -10%);
- the pilot must stay undocked in the system;
- each moon product is reported with its fraction, type ID and moon ID.

Each harvesting module activates only on its own target type, determined from SDE effect and target-group data:
- mining lasers and strip miners: asteroid or moon ore;
- ice harvesters: ice;
- gas cloud harvesters: gas clouds.

A target-type mismatch, or a target beyond the module's max range, is refused with the live UserError and no cycle starts.
